	)
	(text "Controls for additional input signals.\nS3E_* are 'filtered' version of the normal signal.\nWhen ENABLE_S3E is unwanted, then the additional chips are always disabled and all additional address lines to the PMAP and SPMAP SRAMs are zero.\nWhen ENABLE_S3E is wanted, the additional chips track the behavior of those they extend.\n\nexnteded virtual memory (ENABLE_S3E is handled separately to ease debug), as those trea 2 bits also required aliased PMAP to work."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.716 -130.302 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "abd5f72a-d53d-4689-9cc4-e68af989c012")
	)
	(text "The 3/60 is missing the extra 3 bits PA[29..31], the upper 3 of the 19 bits comming out of the PMAP.\nIn the PMAP, the next 5 in the same byte are reserved - let's redefine them as PA[32..36], making the maximum physical space 128 GiB :-)\nDisabled by default, as there's no real need for that much memory.\nCan be designed in/installed (along with the definition of EN.PMAP1 / WE.PMAP1 and the needed bus interface U12) if more than 29 bits of PA are needed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 620.522 153.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "bcfb52ec-7801-423c-b760-07e799278b0b")
	)
	(text "SEGMENT MAP"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.16 -97.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cf468791-5ecb-470c-9155-034e1bdbe5e0")
	)
	(text "U231 needs a bigger PAL (or two PALs)\n(a) it needs to output EN.SMAP1- & WE.SMAP1-\n\nWE_SMAP	 = (            !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nEN_SMAP	 = (            !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & EN_CTL                & C_S5);\n(which ignore alignement) should become\n\n/* byte or upper byte of word */\nWE_SMAP	 = (!A1 & !A0 & !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nEN_SMAP	 = (!A1 & !A0 & !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & EN_CTL                & C_S5);\n/* lower byte of word */\nWE_SMAP1 = (!A1 &  A0 & !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nEN_SMAP1 = (!A1 &  A0 & !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & EN_CTL                & C_S5);\n\n=> this permit to use the extended S[25..31] bits to address more PMAP\n\n(b) it needs access to A31 to alias the SMAP from 0x2 in Control Space to 0x9, oxC and OxD:\n\n/* byte or upper byte of word */\nwe_smap_0x2	 = (!A1 & !A0 & !A28 &  A29 & !A30 & !A31 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nwe_smap_0x9	 = (!A1 & !A0 &  A28 & !A29 & !A30 &  A31 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nwe_smap_0xc	 = (!A1 & !A0 & !A28 & !A29 &  A30 &  A31 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nwe_smap_0xd	 = (!A1 & !A0 &  A28 & !A29 &  A30 &  A31 & EN_CTL & WRITE & C_S3         & !C_S7X);\nWE_SMAP  = we_smap_0x2 | we_smap_0x9 | we_smap_0xc | we_smap_0xd\n\n/* same changes for EN_SMAP, WE_SMAP1, EN_SMAP1 */\n\n=> this also permit to use another 768 MiB of virtual space\n\n(c) it would make sense to also generate EN.PMAP1 and WE.PMAP1 (similar to the other three but with !A1 & A0)\nto support the third bytes of PMAP and the missing PA (PA29 to PA31 architecturally, up to PA36 practically)\n\n**** WARNING ****\nChange (b) requires change in U102 so that EN_CTL is also active for the aliased values,\nas for now U102 enable EN_CTL only if A31==0"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -106.68 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d901f0e3-1e60-4788-9cff-bcc7630bed39")
	)
